command-builtin-editor-enter = New block (or newline in Document mode)
commands-normally-splits-the-current-block-continues-an = Normally splits the current block, continues an in-block list, or adds a sibling note under PDF annotations. In Document mode it inserts a newline unless the Document-mode Enter setting keeps this structural behavior.
command-builtin-editor-soft-newline = Insert a newline inside the block (or new block in Document mode)
command-builtin-editor-escape = Leave editing and select the block
command-builtin-editor-backspace-start = Merge at block start
commands-at-the-start-of-a-block-merges = At the start of a block, merges with the previous block or removes an empty block/list marker.
command-builtin-editor-arrow-cross-block = Move across blocks at visual edges
commands-from-the-first-or-last-visual-row = From the first or last visual row, moves the caret to the previous or next visible block.
command-builtin-editor-copy-block-ref = Copy block reference when no text is selected
command-builtin-editor-paste-plain = Paste as plain text (no formatting conversion)
commands-inserts-the-clipboard-s-plain-text-as-typed = Inserts the clipboard's plain text as typed, inside the current block: HTML structure is ignored and multiline text is not split into blocks. Ordinary paste keeps converting copied web content and outlines.
